We're implementing GitHub issue #802 in the family-tree repo (React+TS frontend at frontend/, FastAPI backend). Working directory: /home/codex/projects/family-tree, on a fresh branch feat/802-tree-selector-shared-section off origin/main.

Issue #802 summary:
The tree switcher dropdown (frontend/src/components/sidebar/DatabaseSelector.tsx) currently renders a single "Trees" SelectGroup containing both owned trees and trees shared with the user (differentiated only by a small Crown/Users icon per row), followed by a separate "Virtual views" SelectGroup (only rendered when virtualViews.length > 0, preceded by a SelectSeparator).

Required change: split the single "Trees" group into two groups — "Your trees" (role === "owner") and "Shared with you" (role !== "owner") — so the dropdown reads top-to-bottom: Your trees → Shared with you → Virtual views. Sections with zero items must be hidden (matching the existing virtual-views pattern of conditional rendering + SelectSeparator). Keep the existing Crown/Users icon per item (lower risk, keeps sort-independent scanability per the issue text).

I already read the current file, full contents below:

```tsx
import {
  Select,
  SelectContent,
  SelectGroup,
  SelectItem,
  SelectLabel,
  SelectSeparator,
  SelectTrigger,
  SelectValue,
} from "@/components/ui/select";
import { SettingsField } from "@/components/sidebar/SettingsField";
